{"title":"2021 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Visual)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Visual)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> be a circle with centre <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> a convex quadrilateral such that each of\nthe segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/e/60eeddb49e38b708d37f0d7be9b741b25050bc6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, BC, CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31cd391bebc36897a8c10ea78e5d584980b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> be the circumcircle of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/7/e277803b04047182e4fc2b0a4771e4521e3936bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AIC$\" width=\"37\" height=\"13\" />.\nThe extension of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66492998689e8303534c9e4f3ba1fa650fd41f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> beyond <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and the extension of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> beyond <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />.\nThe extensions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> beyond <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5b95a8630e3453a008bf566587bb46e413203df.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AD + DT + T X + XA = CD + DY + Y Z + ZC\\]\" width=\"391\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/vUftJHRaNx8\">https://youtu.be/vUftJHRaNx8</a> [Video contains solutions to all day 2 problems]\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U95v_xD5fJk\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U95v_xD5fJk</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/WkdlmduOnRE\">https://youtu.be/WkdlmduOnRE</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the centre of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/4/5f4c25cb7b6078137512af0317bd262160bd0319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=BC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> the result follows simply. By Pitot's Theorem we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/9/439aad77f531aa27111bc5ac31867c15c95e90c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB + CD = BC + AD\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"14\" /> so that, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/a/92a8a2edd8682398cd3a2d4d3564839a5596712a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = CD.$\" width=\"87\" height=\"13\" /> The configuration becomes symmetric about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a2556c5400ea7972b91e9f9154b1604f5995af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OI$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" /> and the result follows immediately.\n</p><p>Now assume WLOG <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/a/8fa537559372da0711df754f5958a463d3fb7771.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB &lt; BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> lies between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> in the minor arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d857b2c804701b561a5c8c90c400f360d27232c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> lies between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in the minor arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/f/aefe76576a63eb4614562452d826f51131557910.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.\nConsider the cyclic quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/f/c4f1a6261f6d419dcb9ba92a64c9ab34316c4603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACZX$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />.\nWe have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6db263f9c7f9e539cec2b7c49e668d04ee60724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CZX = \\angle CAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"139\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d4a79c28f28f1a1d57aa7044ceb73bf72e673d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle IAC = \\angle IZC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"127\" height=\"14\" />. So that, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/d/c4d81b73113f9f76871a0a022e86cf105457da8e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle CZX - \\angle IZC = \\angle CAB - \\angle IAC\\]\" width=\"281\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/a/61a069d28c522500f21b6dbbb66fe15fdcd92583.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle IZX = \\angle IAB\\]\" width=\"125\" height=\"13\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the incenter of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb6f9286d36a1d244aa1be5a7fb0e274d53ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> is the angular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/6/9d64f7c9361e51b0b6cf32335817be5cc9b5b913.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DBA$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />. This gives us, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/2/8f28c03de0542271ac5fdf15bb1c9b6aec915924.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle IZX = \\angle IAB = \\angle IAD = \\angle IAY\\]\" width=\"276\" height=\"13\" /> Hence the chords  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/a/28ac24477884e1fef927e4e541cb138a51af6ff5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IX$\" width=\"25\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/9/9393c74a7cf62ca5920519b811148fb709b48d44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> are equal. \nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a2556c5400ea7972b91e9f9154b1604f5995af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OI$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" />.\nHence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7dcea8808d8ff23374496f64c16101c8a59355.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[TX = YZ\\]\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" /> and now it suffices to prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fd4298fbf98d5c7a4116115566b808ce7544176.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AD + DT + XA = CD + DY + ZC\\]\" width=\"288\" height=\"14\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acb66a5c596974d1b0df5b48324bb3806e168912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P, Q, N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the tangency points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/e/60eeddb49e38b708d37f0d7be9b741b25050bc6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, BC, CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31cd391bebc36897a8c10ea78e5d584980b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Then by tangents we have, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/0/ff010ee32cefe589f79aeab3e9ccad0ef1c85a96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = AM + MD = AP + ND$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"252\" height=\"16\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/3/d738acf53455de9fed868884d43e49f137c593e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD + DT + XA = AP + ND + DT + XA = XP + NT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"451\" height=\"16\" />.\nSimilarly we get, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d9082e23e5b516448d676a5a68bb368bac5fbdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD + DY + ZC = ZQ + YM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"243\" height=\"18\" />. So it suffices to prove, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/5/415a85c85c4181e089c324d3d22f828f8353ccc1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[XP + NT = ZQ + YM\\]\" width=\"191\" height=\"16\" />\nConsider the tangent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/8555c377d982006b09fd42b527987edf36ffdc8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XJ$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a461af1fdd9dcb91f3712f6b2e5555a4994137f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J \\ne P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are reflections about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a2556c5400ea7972b91e9f9154b1604f5995af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OI$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> is a circle centred at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> the tangents <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/8555c377d982006b09fd42b527987edf36ffdc8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XJ$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/81294c38c86bce4a9a53b5f2426c03fc4d25c01d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YM$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> are reflections of each other. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57e46cd8ccb5e9c97fead4d0bc9f5b8d2866a6b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[XP = XJ = YM\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"12\" /> By a similar argument on the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd92d18e856b8ad912223e976294827ef57755bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NT = ZQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> and finally,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/5/415a85c85c4181e089c324d3d22f828f8353ccc1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[XP + NT = ZQ + YM\\]\" width=\"191\" height=\"16\" /> as required.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/4965e3d73b33f66d3c40556be29a9ccdae238e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QED$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>~BUMSTAKA\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> tangents to the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> tangents to the same circle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/03933a7bd92d2cf64844a19ce10785a23f497959.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XB$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> tangents at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/1/a41d471827f400ff9ae3b3c6b336d76a542a285e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ZB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> tangents at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. We can get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/c/24c762ee1bd88b28a12252117e8993906897aa55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=AM+MD;CD=DN+CN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"293\" height=\"18\" />.Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/d/4fdb99adaf10dfa949c8f28df78dc12f7000759d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM=AF,XA=XF-AM;ZC=ZJ-CN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"373\" height=\"18\" /> Same reason, we can get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/d/65d8553af85ca96e4793454b84801c40bc4c1817.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DT=TN-DM;DY=YM-DM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"296\" height=\"18\" />\nWe can find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/c/09cfe01edd5b6f71c994c87cdeee8f8563db8e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD+XA+DT=XF+TN;CD+DY+ZC=ZJ+YM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"488\" height=\"18\" />. Connect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d4810776a24c96764b6dfb1d863b31bdf01407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IM,IT,IT,IZ,IX,IN,IJ,IF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"244\" height=\"18\" /> separately, we can create two pairs of congruent triangles. In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/a/c9a750a7b692cd992a4594160a25e429f1ad99c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{XIF},\\triangle{YIM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc782e14b0c1774e2ae237b08ae12e36ea7276bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{AI}=\\widehat{AI},\\angle{FXI}=\\angle{MYI}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"214\" height=\"23\" /> After getting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/2/de214e9796673c04a05f1b3161b2cc9507b70e25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{IFX}=\\angle{IMY};\\angle{FXI}=\\angle{MYI};IF=IM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"362\" height=\"18\" />, we can find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/0/0100a1aa8ce0958ef11d03e7ee62b8954041b9c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{IFX}\\cong \\triangle{IMY}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />. Getting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d976bf3040849c119329206b0659cdcc34a0d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YM=XF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />, same reason, we can get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/337a561a9aa310d610198dfe1fe9eaae7de51613.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ZJ=TN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />.\nNow the only thing left is that we have to prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/f/e4fb89053ba7fe425b97a6202a59dbf57d21f4b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TX=YZ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/0/a50db5e9ef251b0bc0f50c0709280eb5dedb6dc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{IX}=\\widehat{IY};\\widehat{IT}=\\widehat{IZ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"23\" /> we can subtract and get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/b/08b295da226cefc15436cfd98b4115481f8ce6bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{XT}=\\widehat{YZ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" />,means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c350cb14b6932e33e181c7d521fa2ac1aad4ae5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XT=YZ$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" /> and we are done\n~bluesoul\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Visual.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Visual)\">Solution 3 (Visual)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Visual)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2021_IMO_4b.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/45/2021_IMO_4b.png/420px-2021_IMO_4b.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"420\" height=\"328\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/45/2021_IMO_4b.png/630px-2021_IMO_4b.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/4/45/2021_IMO_4b.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2021_IMO_4.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bf/2021_IMO_4.png/420px-2021_IMO_4.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"420\" height=\"308\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bf/2021_IMO_4.png/630px-2021_IMO_4.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/b/bf/2021_IMO_4.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2021_IMO_4a.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/05/2021_IMO_4a.png/420px-2021_IMO_4a.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"420\" height=\"312\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/05/2021_IMO_4a.png/630px-2021_IMO_4a.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/05/2021_IMO_4a.png/840px-2021_IMO_4a.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>We use the equality of the tangent segments and symmetry.\n</p><p>Using <i><b>Claim 1</b></i> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/738b225c463a67c5ac3a66d29f72d120f85b8cb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {TX}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"24\" /> symmetric to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/1/d7107292b860faa5bb8276170fff174ce19b85a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {ZY}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"24\" /> with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/5/4259a4e6496c5ed7d4890fa06a245c876e7d3ddf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IO.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/b/38b238762d00ee42556667f3a23d1020a27b12e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hspace{10mm} TX = ZY.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"133\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acb66a5c596974d1b0df5b48324bb3806e168912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P, Q, N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the tangency points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/0/e909ddd5ef34b6213a4908bc8957d34f8078667e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, BC, CD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/a/bfaf1de1cd821c3c1698072f3cd91d4594ad9b14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>Using <i><b>Claim 2</b></i> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85faed22434025c2ed61cee6e42a4158839f9f71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TM = QZ, PX = NY.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"182\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/1/69179358405d9378d0456cab357de28efce3f21a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AD + DT + XA = AN+ND + TM – MD +XP-PA =\\]\" width=\"462\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/7/ad74b3bd8ac56f9395ca157c3a488a25678355fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= XP + TM = QZ + NY = MC + ZC + MD + DY =\\]\" width=\"446\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/0/fe0240f6bb9c2a61e7dc75e616738534eb20c30f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=CD + ZC + DY.\\]\" width=\"151\" height=\"14\" />\n<i><b>Claim 1</b></i>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de82b5de37f029271b42d807a7a35ac5a7e8e7b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> Then point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is symmetric to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/f/71f73f86f1061747c66c3ce1d23c43e561d43114.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IO,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is symmetric to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/5/4259a4e6496c5ed7d4890fa06a245c876e7d3ddf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IO.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3c5fe618f80352f5d3f2cfaaa80220badd796bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD =2\\alpha, \\angle ABC =2\\beta, \\angle BCD =2\\gamma, \\angle ADC =2\\delta.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"431\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We find measure of some arcs:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d681387a7520dcb64fd377e3bd9a2f0261d651f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {IT}= 2\\angle ICT = 2\\gamma,\\]\" width=\"153\" height=\"24\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/58655dd82225c346ef65f58cc39d97a865581aa6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {IY}= 2\\angle IAY = 2\\alpha,\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"24\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb99b1348caa6dd691c3376dd389488d974367b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {XY}= 2\\angle XAY = 2\\pi - 4\\alpha,\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"24\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/8/4680942e4393e804373de2be1994534c1b5fd0ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {IX}= 2\\pi - \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {IY} - \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {XY} = 2\\alpha =\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {IY}\\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"309\" height=\"25\" /> symmetry <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/51699aeac52c7ea992acf29d1e92aadd5017be2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y.$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/a/abaf8b3da76ab20464c4dc19363da4ba67be1019.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {TZ}= 2\\angle DCZ = 2\\pi – 4\\gamma,\\]\" width=\"193\" height=\"24\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b45503c0c09e0524a0c6319b9784bdf3c0f1044.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {IZ}= 2\\pi - \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {IT} - \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {TZ}= 2\\gamma= \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {IT}\\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"298\" height=\"27\" /> symmetry <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/7/d4704e108090b4cfc250be3ad235b614bf520530.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z.$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Claim 2</b></i>\n</p><p>Let circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be given. Let points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> lies on  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be symmetric to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/4/f54b14865df28ab0b190757a3183974eadffc9ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OI.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/c/22cf0fa25e560981109abb13757436b94fadb035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> be tangents to  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/1/3a1318eaa23452485935e02679d6a2069ba3b21b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = A&#39;B.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/c/c5c68fdb99644e8535b741e6f6afa4765ba26c63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AI = A&#39;I, IB = IC, \\angle ACI = \\angle A&#39;BI = 90^\\circ \\implies\\]\" width=\"380\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef2921f1275f326bb64e6af5e529266877f46c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\triangle AIC = \\triangle A&#39;IB \\implies A&#39;B = AC.\\]\" width=\"272\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_IMO\" title=\"2021 IMO\">2021 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2021 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink se